gantt - a fast, lightweight replacement for Apache Ant, written in C

Gantt parses standard Ant build.xml files and executes their targets.  Core
tasks (javac, java, jar, javadoc, property handling, Ivy dependency
resolution and more) are built in; file operations and archive tasks are
small helper executables named gantt_<task> that gantt finds through PATH.

Building and installing
=======================

  ./configure
  make
  make check
  make install

Building from a git checkout needs autoconf and automake; run ./autogen.sh
first to create configure.  See INSTALL for the general instructions on
running configure, and README.md for the requirements (a C compiler and
the Expat XML library), usage and the design in more detail.

gantt and its helper executables are all installed into $(bindir)
(/usr/local/bin by default), so nothing beyond having that directory on
your PATH is required.

